Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:34:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vmm: memory in whole host pages (16 KiB on Apple silicon)

Why: macOS on Apple silicon has 16 KiB pages; upstream assumes 4 KiB in a
few places.

What: test memory is laid out in whole host pages, the balloon releases
whole host pages, and the userfaultfd page size is the host page size.
Guest-visible layout is unchanged.

Test: vmm unit tests on a 16 KiB-page host; balloon inflate/deflate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
